 "says": "A repository knowledge source is registered and its first revision (a rate table) is committed. The author checks a domain model for it with knowledge.member.prepare: two nodes, taxable_income and income_tax, and a relation computed_from between them. The owner returns the model exactly as it will be committed, both ends of its one relation naming nodes of that model, and a second revision holding the table and that model is committed on the first head. The author then edits the model to delete the taxable_income node while computed_from still points at it, and checks it against the second head: the owner refuses it with model_reference_dangling and returns no model, so no knowledge_model whose relation names a node it lacks is ever written or committed. The relation-endpoint rule (C04/relation_endpoints_are_nodes) is held by every model the owner returns here; its breaking records stay in the rule fixture.",
 "spec_sha256": "85cb3a0ba9c8e7d70306bec52ff6b66ea6e4531cf5fb09e28e178864ab62d5b4",
